The field's turf textures (lane V2). Made by tools/assets/field/fetch_field_assets.py.

T_Turf_Color.jpg, T_Turf_Normal.jpg and T_Turf_ORM.png are from ambientCG (ambientcg.com),
released under CC0 1.0 Universal (creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/): dedicated to the
public domain, free to use, change and redistribute for any purpose, with no attribution required.
They are credited here anyway.

File(s)                    ambientCG asset              Author        What was done
T_Turf_Color.jpg           Grass 005 (Grass005_2K-JPG)  ambientCG     Kept byte for byte (Grass005_2K-JPG_Color.jpg)
T_Turf_Normal.jpg          Grass 005                    ambientCG     Kept byte for byte (Grass005_2K-JPG_NormalDX.jpg, DirectX convention)
T_Turf_ORM.png             Grass 005                    ambientCG     Packed: R = _AmbientOcclusion.jpg, G = _Roughness.jpg, B = 0 (no metal)

The asset's page is ambientcg.com/view?id=Grass005. The downloaded archive's SHA-256 is pinned in
the script (89183d8dceabc3c23a26978f426e1662143dd2f84f1dc3586a1592d101e5234b).

T_Turf_Noise.png and turf.json are this repository's own, generated by the same script from a
fixed seed and the colour map's pixels (no third-party image goes into the noise), under the
repository's licence.
